The Council of Ireland, established under the Government of Ireland Act 1920 (which was a successor to the Home Rule Bills and addressed all-Ireland governance), had **41 members**. Its composition included:  
- 13 members from each of the Houses of Commons of Southern Ireland and Northern Ireland;  
- 7 members from each of the Senates of Southern Ireland and Northern Ireland;  
- One President chosen by the Lord-Lieutenant of Ireland.  

This body was intended as an all-Ireland law-making authority with limited jurisdiction but never formally met and was abolished in 1925.

Prince Alexey Fyodorovich Orlov participated in the Napoleonic Wars until the capture of Paris in 1814. The outcome of this event was:  
1. Napoleon Bonaparte was forced to abdicate unconditionally on April 6, 1814;  
2. He was exiled to the island of Elba;  
3. The Bourbon monarchy was restored in France with King Louis XVIII ascending the throne.
